      "writtenOn": "2020-03-10T15:48:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "all variable but the swap_cmd could be set here (instead of the caller)\n\n---\n\nAlso, another possibility is to create sub-states for each of these swaps, and the caller just set_state to the correct send state. Each send state (e.g. PE_SEND_DR_SWAP, PE_SEND_PR_SWAP, PD_SEND_VCONN_SWAP) would set the swap_cmd appropriately. Also, the print_state would be more informative.\n\nI would image that only the send states would be expanded, the remaining states could/should be shared.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4378,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 4378,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "2b8a8ccf302c0d428d390e6238df07169f386028",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fcf50c15_15259c1d",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 4378,
      "author": {
        "id": 1149894
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-11T05:34:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The only other variable to initialize is the wait_retry_counter and it should not be set here because this state could be entered several times due to a resend condition.",
      "parentUuid": "c2dcfc8d_03c10684",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4378,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 4378,
        "endChar": 37
